From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: output duplication, display surface data, gamma control, overlay and statistics queries

IDXGIOutput1::DuplicateOutput and IDXGIOutput5::DuplicateOutput1 returned
E_NOTIMPL, so screen capture through the Desktop Duplication API failed. They
now return an IDXGIOutputDuplication for a Direct3D 11 device: the display
image of the output is captured through its display device context into a
B8G8R8A8 texture of the device. AcquireNextFrame waits until the contents change
or the timeout ends (DXGI_ERROR_WAIT_TIMEOUT), frames must be released
(DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL otherwise), the whole screen is the dirty rectangle of
a new frame, there are no move rectangles and no pointer shape, and
MapDesktopSurface is DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED as for a desktop in video memory.
DuplicateOutput1 requires B8G8R8A8_UNORM among the formats it is given.

GetDisplaySurfaceData and GetDisplaySurfaceData1 copy the display into a
surface of the display's size and B8G8R8A8 format (DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL for
others). GetGammaControl reads the display's gamma ramp (identity when it has
none). Output GetFrameStatistics and SetDisplaySurface answer
DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL as without a full-screen owner, and the overlay support
queries report no overlay support.
